              }
            ],
            "text": "In **Massachusetts**, the current maximum regular unemployment benefit is **$1,105 per week**.\n\nYou can receive benefits for **up to 30 weeks**, so the maximum total regular unemployment you could collect is:\n\n**$1,105 \u00d7 30 = $33,150**\n\nYour actual amount is usually about **50% of your average weekly wage**, capped at that $1,105 weekly maximum. Massachusetts may also add a **dependency allowance of up to $25 per eligible child**, but other income or deductions can reduce what you receive. ([mass.gov](https://www.mass.gov/info-details/how-unemployment-insurance-benefits-are-determined?utm_source=openai))",
